Linux 6.x gave two errno values second names: EFSBADCRC is EBADMSG and EFSCORRUPTED is EUCLEAN. glibc's
<errno.h> takes its list from the kernel's headers, so both show up here, twice in the errno-to-name table
("initialized field overwritten", an error with -Werror=override-init). Leave them out, as ECANCELLED and
EREFUSED already are. (musl has a list of its own without them, which is why Melon's build never saw this.)

--- a/src/basic/generate-errno-list.sh	2026-11-19 16:22:49.749420991 -0800
+++ b/src/basic/generate-errno-list.sh	2026-11-19 16:22:49.752419992 -0800
@@ -7,5 +7,5 @@
 # ECANCELED and ECONNREFUSED, respectively. Let's drop them.
 
 ${1:?} -dM -include errno.h - </dev/null | \
-       grep -Ev '^#define[[:space:]]+(ECANCELLED|EREFUSED)' | \
+       grep -Ev '^#define[[:space:]]+(ECANCELLED|EREFUSED|EFSBADCRC|EFSCORRUPTED)' | \
        awk '/^#define[ \t]+E[^ _]+[ \t]+/ { print $2; }'
